A||||6||mblackwell||Having bushings put on||||1||
Z||000000||mblackwell||01-18-2001||04:44 PM||||I bought my '88 Formula (my first and only car) for $1500 about 6 months ago.  It has a knocking sound in the front end.  The previous owner said this was the bushings,  he had bought poly bushings but never put them on.  He included them with the car.  How much would it cost to have them put on and have the steering aligned?  I looked under the front end and the bushing area looks pretty rusty.||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||01-18-2001||08:34 PM||||Anyone?||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||01-18-2001||09:51 PM||||Not many people on here had poly installed for them. When I installed mine, it was around $50 for 4-wheel alignment. I don't know what a local shop would charge, but I can guess it would be at least $500 in labor.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||01-18-2001||11:57 PM||||Can't help you on installing the bushings. Most people seem to do it themself. $50 or $60 is about right for the alignment which you will need after the bushings are done. Although the poly bushings will tighten up the suspension, I doubt those bushings are responsible for a knocking sound.<P>I had a knocking sound in my 88 Formula, mostly when the passenger wheel hit a pot hole. It turned out to be the bushing in the end of the rack and pinion unit. It is made of plastic and has a tendency to wear out. Jack up the passenger side, turn the wheel to the left, and see if you can feel any play where the rack comes out of the housing. To tell for sure you may need to take the dust boot loose. There's a picture on the site below that might help clarify what I'm saying.<P>I replaced mine with another GM one for about $20 (part only). Right after that I saw an aluminum one on Rodney's site for about the same price and will try it if I do it again.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com/retail.html</A> <BR>Look under Steering - 88 rack bushing<BR><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 01-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||01-19-2001||08:06 AM||||Mr. Goodwrench wanted $500 for install of bushings.  $60/hr plus bushings.  The mechanics eyes sort of rolled back into his head when I asked to have it done.  I had Twin Lakes do the install last winter when the 87 car was out for mantenance.  The car drove better than when it was new after Bob finished.<P>He's doinig it for the 88 car too.||||reg||3
Z||000005||rodmcneill||01-19-2001||11:47 AM||||Old Lar, how much did Twin Lakes charge for the poly. installation?||||reg||5
Z||000006||Old Lar||01-19-2001||01:19 PM||||I never got a breakdown on prices.  Bob replaced the clutch, bushings, electric door switches, driver's side mirror, Borla Exhaust (I supplied from Tim Perrigo in Maine) seems like other stuff all in the 87.<P>As well as he is swapping in a new 3.4 and new t440 automatic in my 88 plus bushings, brakes, another Borla exhaust, one GT window (I supplied), Nolan concepts chromed throttle body and powder coated intake manifold plenum and valve covers, plus some paint touch up, and anything else that needs fixing.<P>So I just write checks to Bob.  The 88 will be a brand new car, because I already had new suspension put in 99.<P>I guess I get a large volume discount.||||reg||3
